flowchart TD
    start([Define one feature]) --> clarify[Clarify problem, users and expected value]
    clarify --> specify[Specify behavior, acceptance criteria, scope, non-goals and dependencies]
%% @airflow-context specify
%% Write one independently deliverable feature Definition using the canonical
%% record outline below. Make acceptance criteria observable and
%% testable; record dependencies, constraints, non-goals and unresolved questions.

%% Record path: `.air/features/<feature-id>/definition.md`.
%% Record outline: Proposal source; Problem and user outcome; In scope; Out of scope; Acceptance criteria; Dependencies and constraints; Open questions; Decisions and evidence.
%% Mutable statuses belong in the index. Example IDs and versions are placeholders.
%% @end-airflow-context
    specify --> review[Check boundaries, dependencies and observable acceptance criteria]
    review --> quality{Definition consistent and sufficiently specified?}
    quality -- No: resolvable from available evidence --> specify
    quality -- Missing product decision --> blocked([Blocked: ask focused question])
    quality -- Yes: save reviewed draft --> definitionApproval{Feature definition approved by user?}
%% @airflow-context review
%% Resolve omissions from existing approved context where possible. Ensure each
%% acceptance criterion is observable, scope/non-goals agree, dependencies are
%% explicit and no unresolved question prevents design. Never invent requirements
%% or ask the human to perform this completeness check for the AI.
%% @end-airflow-context
    definitionApproval -- No: ask questions or revise --> clarify
    definitionApproval -- Yes: save feature definition --> definitionReady([Definition approved: return to caller])
    definitionApproval -- Defer --> deferred([Deferred: keep out of release scope])
    definitionApproval -- Reject --> rejected([Rejected: record decision in `.air/index.md`])
%% @airflow-context definitionApproval
%% Initial approval permits backlog entry; revised approval restores selected
%% status only with valid scope membership, using Project impact rules. Bind
%% approval to the exact Definition digest and record its evidence in `.air/index.md`
%% using the global Approval evidence section. Defer/reject decisions are
%% recorded but never included in a release scope.

%% Feature transitions owned by this phase:
%% - `clarifying` -> `backlog`: Human approves the exact Definition; no valid active release membership remains.
%% - `clarifying` -> `selected`: Revised Definition approved; feature remains in a valid approved scope. Revalidate dependent Design before work.
%% - `clarifying` -> `deferred` / `rejected`: Explicit human decision; unapproved Definition stays `draft`. Re-scope any containing release before continuing.
%% - `backlog` / `selected` / `implementing` / `verifying` / `verified` -> `clarifying`: Material Definition change; invalidate its approval and assess dependent scope/Design/checks.
%% @end-airflow-context

    classDef boundary fill:#126a52,color:#ffffff,stroke:#126a52
    classDef approval fill:#fff0e8,color:#633b2c,stroke:#c68162
    class start,definitionReady,deferred,rejected boundary
    class definitionApproval approval
